{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Why Use Object Oriented Programming?"}, {"type": "position", "content": 2}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 1}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear when talking about OOP"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe common simple incidents at work in a simple spoken or written situation with a supportive interlocutor. Build the macro system conceptual model following the customer requirements, through the use and interpretation of collected information, represented in class diagrams, interaction diagrams, and operation contracts."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation. Exchanges simple information on programming tools and solutions to a client's requirement."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob02re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "There is \u2013 There are"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">There is \u2013 There are</span> to talk about the existence of something"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">there is</span> and <span class=\"strong\">there are</span> in simple present tense for affirmative sentences when you want to express the existence of someone or something.</br></br>    <span class=\"strong\">There is</span> is used for singular countable nouns or for uncountable nouns: </br></br>   <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">There is</span> a new software in the company.  </span></br> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">There is</span> some time they give us to learn.</span></br></br>  You can use a contraction for this singular form:</br> <div class=\"center_text\">There is \u2013 There's</div></br></br> <span class=\"strong\">There are</span> is used for  plural countable nouns: </br></br> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">There are</span> issues we have to solve. </span></br> <span class=\"italic\"><span class=\"strong\">There are</span> three specialist who can help us.</span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "There are just three main questions about the same topic."}, {"type": "example", "content": "There is a problem regarding poor analysis and design, and there is another regarding maintainability, right?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Well, there is a reason why it is important to use OOP and it is because OOP can help us overcome common problems in computer system design. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Through OOP, we can make sure there are systems that are easy to maintain and that are robust. "}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Modal Can to Ask for Clarification"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the modal  <span class=\"strong\">can</span> to ask for clarification about any topic."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">Can</span> in different purposes, one of them is to clarify information when you use it in a question. You use modal <span class=\"strong\">can</span> for interrogative sentences using the following structure</br></br>   <div class=\"center_text\">Can + subject + verb + complement +?</div></br></br>    <span class=\"italic\">For example: </span></br>   <span class=\"italic\">Can you help me with this program? </span> </br> <span class=\"italic\">Can you clarify this concept? </span> </br>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Now, can those problems affect OOP?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Can a system be damaged after its initial development phase?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Can you explain why robustness is so important here?"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "maintainability "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "ease with which a product or system can be continually restored  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There is a problem regarding poor analysis and design, and there is another regarding maintainability, right?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob02aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "incur "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to happen"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb): "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example:  Well, since robustness refers to the ability of a system to cope with errors that can incur during its execution, it is the job of software engineers to guarantee a system is robust and, therefore, maintainable. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob02aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "phase "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "stage"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: With OOP, they can analyze and design all the tasks for the development of the software during its initial phase and predict its future behavior. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob02aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "overcome "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to defeat"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Well, there is a reason why it is important to use OOP and it is because OOP can help us overcome common problems in computer system design. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob02aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "robustness "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the ability of a system to continue working in spite of execution or input defaults"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In this sense, there is an important issue we have to keep in mind, system robustness."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le01ob02aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Research about one common problem that occurs when someone designs a software. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Explain in a piece of writing what is the best way to solve that problem."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Ask for an opinion to your teacher or partners about your solution. "}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I research about computer system design."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I propose a solution for a specific problem regarding computer system design."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I share my solution proposal.  "}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "id": 0, "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n2le01ob02re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n2le01ob02re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter: </span> The test is simple. There are just three main questions about the same topic. Let's start by reviewing common problems in computer system designs.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sam: </span> Wait! I know them. There is a problem regarding poor analysis and design, and there is another regarding maintainability, right?</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter: </span> Great! Now, can those problems affect OOP? </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sam: </span> Yes, they can. There are some problems when the system doesn't do the right things, and there are problems when the computer system is hard to understand. In the first case, poor analysis and design are the causes, while poor maintainability is the reason for the second one."}, {"time": "41000", "image": "enpe8n2le01ob02re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter: </span> Ok. So, how can OOP reduce maintenance problems? </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sam: </span> Well, there is a reason why it is important to use OOP and it is because OOP can help us overcome common problems in computer system design. In other words, software engineers need to make sure the software they design is easy to maintain throughout the years after its initial creation; they can achieve this by using OOP properly. With OOP, they can analyze and design all the tasks for the development of the software during its initial phase and predict its future behavior.  </br>"}, {"time": "81000", "image": "enpe8n2le01ob02re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Peter: </span> Now that you mention it. Can a system be damaged after its initial development phase? </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sam: </span> Sure! They can be caused by the changes that companies do for its development. In this sense, there is an important issue we have to keep in mind, system robustness.</br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter: </span> Can you explain why robustness is so important here? </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sam: </span> Well, since robustness refers to the ability of a system to cope with errors that can incur during its execution, it is the job of software engineers to guarantee a system is robust and, therefore, maintainable. Through OOP, we can make sure there are systems that are easy to maintain and that are robust. These two features guarantee a system's appropriate functioning.  </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Peter: </span> Well done! I think we're now ready for the test. </br>\n<span class=\"strong\">Sam: </span> Of course we are!"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n2le01ob02re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimul